###############################################################################
# "Library" OData V4 test model - known limits and deviations
#
# Start the server first:  dotnet run --project src/LibraryService
# Every request carries the result actually observed against .NET 10.0 with
# Microsoft.AspNetCore.OData 9.5.0.
#
# These are the requests that do NOT answer the way the OData spec or the
# reference model would suggest. Each is separated by cause: the persistence
# layer, the library, or this implementation. See ../FEATURE-COVERAGE.md for
# the reasoning; this file only keeps the behaviour observable.
#
# The persistence layer has almost nothing left in here. It used to carry the
# whole Edm.DateTimeOffset section - SQLite has no type for a timestamp, a
# decimal or a duration, so all three were stored as integers and the date-part
# functions over them either failed or answered wrongly. Postgres has all
# three, and those requests now belong in query-options.http.
###############################################################################

@host = http://localhost:5091/odata/v4/library
@audiobook = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@book = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@loan = 88888888-8888-8888-8888-888888888888

###############################################################################
# This implementation: only UTC timestamps are accepted
#
# A deliberate deviation. Edm.DateTimeOffset permits any offset and a fully
# conformant server round-trips +02:00 unchanged; this one refuses it, because
# UTC on the wire and at rest is the sane way to run a service and the whole
# reference model is UTC already. It is refused rather than silently converted,
# so that the client's value is never quietly reinterpreted.
###############################################################################

### 400 - non-UTC offset in a write
PATCH {{host}}/Members(2)
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ActiveSince": "2021-01-01T12:00:00+02:00" }

### 400 - and the same in a $filter literal, through the same guard
GET {{host}}/Loans?$filter=LoanedAt gt 2020-01-01T00:00:00+02:00

### 204 - the same instant as UTC is accepted
PATCH {{host}}/Members(2)
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ActiveSince": "2021-01-01T10:00:00Z" }

###############################################################################
# The library: $compute=date(...) does not truncate
#
# The declared type is Edm.Date, but the whole timestamp comes back. In $filter
# the same function is correct - see query-options.http, where eq, ne, ge and
# le all answer as they should - so this is $compute's projection alone.
###############################################################################

### 200 - "D": "2026-06-01T10:00:00Z", where a date was declared
GET {{host}}/Loans?$compute=date(LoanedAt) as D&$select=Id,D

###############################################################################
# The persistence layer: the spatial types are stored as WKT text
#
# EF Core's spatial support is NetTopologySuite-only and would additionally
# want PostGIS, so the type system OData speaks - Microsoft.Spatial - has no EF
# provider at all. Deliberately out of scope - see CLAUDE.md.
###############################################################################

### 400 - Unknown function 'geo.distance'. Not reached by the store at all:
### ODL's own query binder does not implement the geo.* functions.
GET {{host}}/Branches?$filter=geo.distance(Location,geography'SRID=4326;Point(13.4 52.5)') lt 10000

### 200 - the values themselves round-trip exactly, SRID included:
### "crs": {"name": "EPSG:4326"}
GET {{host}}/Branches(1)

###############################################################################
# The persistence layer: dynamic properties are stored as JSON
###############################################################################

### 200 - the open type's dynamic properties are served
GET {{host}}/Media(77777777-7777-7777-7777-777777777777)

### 400 - but they can never appear in $filter or $orderby: they are not
### declared on the type, so the URI parser refuses them before the store is
### ever asked
GET {{host}}/Media?$filter=Appraisal gt 1000

###############################################################################
# The library: Edm.Duration has no date-part functions either
###############################################################################

### 400 - Unknown function 'totalseconds'
GET {{host}}/Media/Library.Catalog.Audiobook?$filter=totalseconds(Duration) gt 100

###############################################################################
# This implementation: the HTTP preconditions are not enforced
#
# Copy/Condition is annotated Core.OptimisticConcurrency, is emitted as
# @odata.etag, and EF puts the original value into the WHERE of every UPDATE -
# so two writers racing on one copy do collide. The HTTP half is missing: the
# controllers never read If-Match.
###############################################################################

### 204 - a stale ETag is accepted; 412 is never returned
PATCH {{host}}/Copies(MediumId={{book}},InventoryNumber=1)
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: W/"AAAA"

{ "Condition": 5 }

###############################################################################
# This implementation: addressing gaps
###############################################################################

### 404 - a single contained entity by key is not served. Only the collection
### and the chapter's stream are, see read.http and streams.http.
GET {{host}}/Media({{audiobook}})/Library.Catalog.Audiobook/Chapters(1)

### 404 - $entity?$id= is not routed
GET {{host}}/$entity?$id=Media({{book}})
